)F FUNCTION -                                                           00050000
  THE TERMINAL COMMAND IS USED TO DEFINE THE PHYSICAL TERMINAL          00100000
  CHARACTERSTICS TO THE TSO SYSTEM. THESE CHARACTERISTICS APPLY TO      00150000
  THE TERMINAL CURRENTLY IN USE AND ARE VALID FOR ONLY ONE SESSION      00200000
  OR UNTIL THE TERMINAL COMMAND IS REISSUED DURING THE SESSION.         00250000
)X SYNTAX -                                                             00300000
         TERMINAL   LINES('INTEGER')/NOLINES                            00350000
                    SECONDS('INTEGER')/NOSECONDS                        00352000
                    INPUT('CHARACTER STRING')/NOINPUT                   00400000
                    LINESIZE('INTEGER')/SCRSIZE('N','M')                00450020
                    BREAK/NOBREAK  TIMEOUT/NOTIMEOUT                    00460000
                    CLEAR('CHARACTER STRING')/NOCLEAR                   00500000
                    TRAN('NAME')/NOTRAN                                 00530003
                    CHAR((X'HEXCHAR',C'CHAR'),...)/NOCHAR               00560003
  REQUIRED - NONE                                                       00600000
  DEFAULTS - NONE                                                       00650000
  ALIAS    - TERM                                                       00660000
  NOTE     - IF THE TERMINAL COMMAND IS ENTERED WITH NO OPERANDS, THE   00700000
             COMMAND IS IGNORED.                                        00750000
  NOTE     - SOME OF THE TERMINAL COMMAND KEYWORDS ARE NOT SUPPORTED    00760003
             ON ALL TERMINAL TYPES.                                     00770003
)O OPERANDS-                                                            00800000
))LINES('INTEGER')                                                      00850000
           - SPECIFIES THE MAXIMUM NUMBER OF CONTINUOUS OUTPUT WHICH    00900020
             IS TO OCCUR BETWEEN PROMPTS FOR A SIMULATED ATTENTION.     00950000
    'INTEGER'                                                           01000000
           - MUST BE A VALUE FROM 1-255.                                01050000
))NOLINES  - SPECIFIES THAT PROMPTING FOR SIMULATED ATTENTIONS TO       01100020
             INTERRUPT OUTPUT WILL BE TERMINATED.                       01150000
))SECONDS('INTEGER')                                                    01200000
           - SPECIFIES THE MAXIMUM AMOUNT OF 'LOCKED KEYBOARD' TIME     01250020
             (ALL NUMBERS ARE ROUNDED TO THE NEAREST TEN SECONDS)       01300000
             WHICH IS TO OCCUR BETWEEN PROMPTS FOR SIMULATED            01350000
             ATTENTIONS.                                                01400000
    'INTEGER'                                                           01450000
           - MUST BE A VALUE FROM 10 TO 2550.                           01500000
))NOSECONDS- SPECIFIES THAT THE USER IS NOT TO BE PROMPTED FOR          01550020
             SIMULATED ATTENTIONS WHEN HIS KEYBOARD WOULD               01600000
             ORDINARILY BE LOCKED AND HIS TERMINAL INACTIVE.            01650000
))INPUT('CHARACTER STRING')                                             01700000
           - SPECIFIES A CHARACTER STRING WHICH IS TO BE RECOGNIZED     01750000
             DURING INPUT OPERATIONS AS AN ATTENTION.                   01800000
    'CHARACTER STRING'                                                  01850000
           - IS ANY COMBINATION OF 4 OR LESS VALID CHARACTERS.          01900000
))NOINPUT  - SPECIFIES THAT NO CHARACTER STRING WILL BE USED FOR        01950000
             ATTENTION ON INPUT.                                        02000000
))LINESIZE('INTEGER')                                                   02050000
           - SPECIFIES THE MAXIMUM NUMBER OF CHARACTERS THAT ARE TO     02100000
             BE PRINTED ON A LINE AT A KEYBOARD TYPE TERMINAL.          02150000
    'INTEGER'                                                           02200000
           - IS A VALUE FROM 1 TO 255.                                  02250020
))SCRSIZE('N','M')                                                      02300020
           - SPECIFIES THE DIMENSION OF THE DISPLAY STATION.            02350000
    'N'    - SPECIFIES THE NUMBER OF ROWS ON THE SCREEN.                02400000
    'M'    - SPECIFIES THE LENGTH OF EACH ROW.                          02450000
))BREAK    - SPECIFIES THAT THE TERMINAL HAS THE REVERSE BREAK FEATURE. 02500000
))NOBREAK  - SPECIFIES THAT THE TERMINAL DOES NOT HAVE THE REVERSE      02550000
             BREAK FEATURE.                                             02600000
))TIMEOUT  - SPECIFIES THAT THE TERMINAL DOES NOT HAVE THE TIMEOUT      02650000
             SUPPRESSION FEATURE: WHEN IN TRANSMIT MODE, THE KEYBOARD   02700000
             WILL LOCK IF THE USER DOES NOT STRIKE A KEY WITHIN         02750000
             APPROXIMATELY 9-18 SECONDS. OF THE TERMINALS SUPPORTED     02800000
             FOR FIRST RELEASE, THIS OPERAND IS APPLICABLE ONLY TO      02850000
             1050 AND NEED BE USED ONLY IF THE INSTALLATION HAS         02900000
             DEFINED THE TERMINAL OR THE LINE ON WHICH IT MAY CALL      02950000
             THE CPU AS HAVING THE TEXT TIMEOUT SUPPRESSION FEATURE.    03000000
))NOTIMEOUT- SPECIFIES THAT THE TERMINAL DOES HAVE THE TIMEOUT          03050000
             SUPPRESSION FEATURE.                                       03100000
))CLEAR('CHARACTER STRING')                                             03150000
           - SPECIFIES A CHARACTER STRING TO BE USED TO CLEAR THE       03200000
             SCREEN OF THE DISPLAY STATION.                             03250000
    'CHARACTER STRING'                                                  03300000
           - IS A COMBINATION OF 4 OR LESS VALID CHARACTERS.            03330003
))NOCLEAR  - SPECIFIES THAT A CHARACTER STRING WILL NOT BE USED         03400000
             TO ERASE THE SCREEN OF A DISPLAY STATION.                  03450000
))TRAN('NAME')                                                          03500003
           - CHARACTER CODE TRANSLATION IS IN EFFECT USING THE          03550003
             TABLES CONTAINED IN THE LOAD MODULE SPECIFIED.             03580003
    'NAME' - THE LOAD MODULE NAME THAT CONTAINS THE TRANSLATE TABLE.    03610003
))NOTRAN   - SPECIFIES THAT NO CHARACTER TRANSLATION IS TO TAKE PLACE.  03700003
))CHAR((X'HEXCHAR',C'CHAR'),(C'CHAR',X'HEXCHAR'),...)                   03750003
           - SPECIFIES ONE OR MORE PAIRS OF CHARACTERS, IN EITHER       03800003
             HEXADECIMAL OR CHARACTER NOTATION, THAT REPLACE            03850003
             CHARACTERS IN THE TRANSLATE TABLE.                         03900003
    '(X'HEXCHAR',C'CHAR'),(C'CHAR',X'HEXCHAR'),...'                     03906003
           - THE FIRST CHARACTER OF THE PAIR IS THE CURRENT             03912003
             CHARACTER THAT IS DEFINED. THE SECOND CHARACTER            03918003
             IS THE NEW CHARACTER THAT IS TO REPLACE THE                03924003
             FIRST ONE.                                                 03930003
             EITHER THE FIRST OR THE SECOND CHARACTER MAY BE            03936003
             EXPRESSED IN HEXADECIMAL OR CHARACTER NOTATION.            03942003
))NOCHAR   - SPECIFIES THAT ALL CHARACTER TRANSLATIONS PREVIOUSLY       03950003
             SPECIFIED ARE NO LONGER IN EFFECT.                         04000003
